# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known, by-design allocations in QuarkDB.
# Each of these allocates its helper objects once with `new` and never frees
# them (the classes have no destructors). On a device QuarkDB is a global
# that lives forever, so this is harmless there. Anything not listed here
# that leaks still fails the test run.
# Remove an entry once the matching class gets a destructor.
leak:QuarkDB::init
leak:DBReadProcessor::DBReadProcessor
leak:DBWriteProcessor::DBWriteProcessor
leak:DBFilterProcessor::DBFilterProcessor
leak:CommandParser::CommandParser
